{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.QCasimir","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.QCasimir","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CasimirShared","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.Order.Field","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Filter.Basic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":31,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimirEigenvalue_weyl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimirEigenvalue_weyl","kind":"theorem","line":648,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L648-L660","doc":"The q-Casimir eigenvalue is symmetric under `j ↦ -(j+1)`:\n`[j]_q · [j+1]_q = [-(j+1)]_q · [-j]_q`, using `[-n]_q = -[n]_q`.\nReflects the Weyl-symmetry `j ↔ -j-1` of `j(j+1)` in the\nclassical limit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qNumberSym_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qNumberSym_neg","kind":"theorem","line":639,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L639-L646","doc":"Negation-antisymmetry of the symmetric q-number: `[-n]_q = -[n]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimirEigenvalue_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimirEigenvalue_zero","kind":"theorem","line":630,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L630-L637","doc":"Sanity check: the eigenvalue on the trivial representation `V_0`\nvanishes — exactly the normalisation chosen in `QCasimir`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qNumberSym_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qNumberSym_zero","kind":"theorem","line":625,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L625-L628","doc":"Sanity check: `[0]_q = 0` in the symmetric convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimirEigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimirEigenvalue","kind":"def","line":611,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L611-L623","doc":"Eigenvalue of the q-Casimir on the integer-spin irreducible `V_j`.\n\nOn the highest-weight module `V_j` (with convention\n`K v_j = q^{2j} v_j`), the normalised q-Casimir acts as the\nscalar `[j]_q · [j+1]_q`.  For half-integer spins, reparametrise\nusing `q^{1/2}` (Kassel §VI.4); the integer case below handles\nthe representation-theoretic content after this reparametrisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qNumberSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qNumberSym","kind":"def","line":601,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L601-L609","doc":"Symmetric q-number over any field: `[n]_q = (qⁿ - q⁻ⁿ)/(q - q⁻¹)`.\nRequires `q ≠ 0` implicitly (via `zpow`) and `q² ≠ 1` for the\ndenominator to be nonzero.  Distinguish from the asymmetric\n`QuantumSu2.qInt` (`(qⁿ - 1)/(q - 1)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimir_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimir_central","kind":"theorem","line":577,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L577-L586","doc":"**Full centrality of the q-Casimir** — packaged as a theorem.\nCombines `QCasimir_comm_E`, `QCasimir_comm_F`, `QCasimir_comm_K`\ninto the statement that `C_q` commutes with every generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimir_comm_F","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimir_comm_F","kind":"theorem","line":569,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L569-L575","doc":"`QCasimir` commutes with `F`.  Symmetric to `QCasimir_comm_E`\nunder the involution `E ↔ F`, `q ↔ q⁻¹`, `K ↔ K⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimir_comm_F_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimir_comm_F_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":562,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L562-L567","doc":"**External axiom (Kassel 1995 §VI.4):** QCasimir commutes with F\n(symmetric to QCasimir_comm_E under E↔F). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimir_comm_E","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimir_comm_E","kind":"theorem","line":552,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L552-L555","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimir_comm_E_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimir_comm_E_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":543,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L543-L549","doc":"**External axiom (Kassel 1995 §VI.4):** QCasimir commutes with E.\nSubstantive Hecke-algebra calc chain via K_cancel / K_inv_cancel\nidentities, pending the full ring-arithmetic Lean port. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.W_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.W_central","kind":"theorem","line":514,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L514-L523","doc":"W := `invQm · invQm` is central in `qs.Algebra`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.K_inv_mul_F","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.K_inv_mul_F","kind":"theorem","line":493,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L493-L512","doc":"Auxiliary: `K_inv · F = ι(q²) · F · K_inv`.  Mirror of `K_mul_F`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.K_inv_mul_E","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.K_inv_mul_E","kind":"theorem","line":472,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L472-L491","doc":"Auxiliary: `K_inv · E = ι(q⁻²) · E · K_inv`.  Mirror of `K_mul_E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.K_inv_cancel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.K_inv_cancel","kind":"theorem","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L454-L470","doc":"The \"K_inv-cancellation\" lemma: `ι(qInv³-qInv)·invQm² = -ι(qInv²)·invQm`.\nMirror of `K_cancel` used for the `E·K_inv` terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.K_cancel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.K_cancel","kind":"theorem","line":439,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L439-L452","doc":"The \"K-cancellation\" lemma: `ι(q³-q)·invQm² = ι(q²)·invQm`.\nUsed in E-centrality to cancel the `E·K` terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qInv_cubed_minus_qInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qInv_cubed_minus_qInv","kind":"theorem","line":426,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L426-L435","doc":"`q⁻³ - q⁻¹ = -(q⁻² · (q - q⁻¹))`: mirror of `q_cubed_minus_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_cubed_minus_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_cubed_minus_q","kind":"theorem","line":414,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L414-L424","doc":"`q³ - q = q² · (q - q⁻¹)`.  A plain ring identity in `R_q`\nusing `qInv_right`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.F_mul_K_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.F_mul_K_inv","kind":"theorem","line":392,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L392-L410","doc":"`F · K_inv = ι(q⁻²) · (K_inv · F)`: dual of `E_mul_K_inv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.E_mul_K_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.E_mul_K_inv","kind":"theorem","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L369-L390","doc":"`E · K_inv = ι(q²) · (K_inv · E)`: derived from `K_mul_E` by\nconjugating with `K_inv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.F_mul_K","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.F_mul_K","kind":"theorem","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L349-L367","doc":"`F · K = ι(q²) · (K · F)`: dual of `K_mul_F`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.E_mul_K","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.E_mul_K","kind":"theorem","line":328,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L328-L347","doc":"`E · K = ι(q⁻²) · (K · E)`: the dual of `K_mul_E` obtained by\nmultiplying both sides by `ι(q⁻²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimir_comm_K","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimir_comm_K","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L265-L324","doc":"**K-centrality**: the q-Casimir commutes with `K`.\n\nCombines `FE_comm_K` with the manifest K-centrality of the scalar\npart.  The `(q·K + q⁻¹·K⁻¹ - (q+q⁻¹))` factor commutes with `K`\nbecause each summand is built from `K`, `K⁻¹`, and `ι`-scalars\n(which are central).  `invQm` is central by hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FE_comm_K","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FE_comm_K","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L189-L263","doc":"**FE commutes with K** (auxiliary for K-centrality).  From\n`K_mul_E` and `K_mul_F`, the q-twists cancel: `K(FE) = q⁻²q²(FE)K\n= (FE)K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimir_eq_EF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimir_eq_EF","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L126-L185","doc":"**EF/FE equivalence**: `QCasimir = QCasimir_EF`.\n\nDerivation.  Let `Δ := (qK + q⁻¹K⁻¹) - (q⁻¹K + qK⁻¹) = (q-q⁻¹)(K - K⁻¹)`,\nThe difference of the bracketed parts equals `ι(q-q⁻¹)·(K-K⁻¹)`.\nMultiplying by `invQm · invQm` and using `invQm_right` once,\n\n`Δ · invQm · invQm = ι(q-q⁻¹) · (K - K⁻¹) · invQm · invQm`\n                 ` = (K - K⁻¹) · (ι(q-q⁻¹) · invQm) · invQm`\n                 ` = (K - K⁻¹) · invQm`,\n\nwhich by `E_F_comm` equals `EF - FE`.  Thus\n`FE + bracket_FE · invQm² = EF - (EF - FE) + bracket_FE · invQm²\n                         = EF + bracket_EF · invQm²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QCasimir_EF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QCasimir_EF","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L113-L124","doc":"The dual `EF`-form of `C_q`: applying the commutator\n`[E,F] = (K - K⁻¹) · (q - q⁻¹)⁻¹` to the leading `FE` term yields\n\n`C_q = E·F + (q⁻¹·K + q·K⁻¹ - (q + q⁻¹)) · (q - q⁻¹)⁻²`.\n\nThis dual presentation is convenient for highest-weight calculations\n(where `E v_j = 0`).  Provable directly from `QuantumSu2Relations`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2Relations.E_F_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumSu2Relations.E_F_comm","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L104-L104","doc":"`[E, F] = (K − K⁻¹) · (q − q⁻¹)⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2Relations.K_mul_F","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumSu2Relations.K_mul_F","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L102-L102","doc":"`K · F = q⁻² · F · K` (equivalently `K F K⁻¹ = q⁻² F`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2Relations.K_mul_E","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumSu2Relations.K_mul_E","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L100-L100","doc":"`K · E = q² · E · K` (equivalently `K E K⁻¹ = q² E`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2Relations.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumSu2Relations.mk","kind":"ctor","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L98-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumSu2Relations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumSu2Relations","kind":"class","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/q-casimir.lean#L90-L104","doc":"The structural q-relations of 𝒰_q(𝔰𝔲(2)) that are *not* recorded\nin the bare `QuantumSu2` skeleton (which only knows about\n`K · K⁻¹ = 1`).  Carry these as a typeclass so that `QCasimir`\nproperties can be derived from the same Hopf presentation Kassel\nuses in §VI.4. ","signatureChunk":0}]}